==========================================================================================
H4 -- THE COST d(H2-H3) CANNOT SEE
==========================================================================================
  d(H2-H3) is blind to H4 by construction, and H4 is not a free ride: at the low
  anchor the model already sits ABOVE ND on H4 while sitting BELOW it on H2, so a
  lever that raises both improves one and worsens the other
  (`difference-statistics-hide-common-mode`).

  ⚠⚠ BUT THIS ROW HAS NEVER BEEN GUARDED, AND THE ANCHOR SUBSET DOES NOT GUARD IT
  (session 83).  `msub`/`nsub` select on `ok23` -- H2 AND H3 measurable -- because
  the headline statistic is the H2-H3 pair.  `ok45` is computed per hit and is
  simply never consulted here, so every H4 number printed since session 80 is a
  median over cells selected for H2/H3 reliability and NOT for H4's.  That matters
  because a floored Hn is not a measurement: the LS fit returns whatever noise
  projects onto that basis vector, bounded BELOW by roughly the cell's residual, so
  a floored value reads too HIGH.  On the MODEL side that biases (model - ND)
  UPWARD -- which is exactly the direction of the claim being made.  The support
  and the reference-guarded read are therefore printed below, and the guard is on
  the REFERENCE (`floor-guard-belongs-on-the-reference`, session 74 item 6 --
  guarding on the model selects away the cells where the model under-produces).
